course: dictionary
lesson: 3240
title: Picturing the future
level: primary-5
stars: 3
explain: To envision something is to picture it in your mind, often something that has not happened yet. You can envision a holiday, a new bike, or a playground you would love to build.
explain: To envision a plan means you expect or hope it will happen in a certain way. In «NASA's DAVINCI and VERITAS missions and Europe's EnVision have been planned to visit Venus in the 2030s», the words «in the 2030s» are a clue that the thinking is about the future. EnVision is also the name of one mission, but the idea behind the word is still picturing what will happen.
explain: Look for clue words around envision. Words like «future», «perfect» or «how» show that someone is imagining what could happen. When you meet a new word, try putting your own meaning in its place: "They picture a future visit to Venus" still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
fact: Envision means to imagine or picture something in your mind.
fact: Envision often points to the future, as in «envision your perfect playground».
fact: To envision a plan means to expect or hope it will happen in a certain way.
fact: UK English often uses envisage, which means the same as envision.
fact: The verb forms are envision, envisions, envisioned and envisioning.
exercise: «Maya tries to envision her perfect playground.» What does envision mean here? | Dig it up with a spade | Count how many swings it has | *Picture it in her mind | Forget it completely
exercise: «The team hopes to envision a greener town by 2040.» Which words are the best clue that this is about the future? | town | hopes | team | *by 2040
exercise: Which word means the same as envision in UK English? | enter | *envisage | envy | envelope
test: «Scientists envision a new spacecraft reaching Venus one day.» What is the best meaning of envision? | Measure how big it is | *Imagine or picture it in your mind | Stop it from happening | Sell something cheaply
test: Last summer Ali envisioned a rocket landing on Mars. Which form of the verb is this? | envision | envisions | *envisioned | envisioning
exam: «The scientists envision a new spacecraft visiting Venus, though the dates keep changing.» What does envision mean? | Pay for the spacecraft | Forget the plan completely | *Picture or imagine it in your mind | Measure the distance exactly
